    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d930">

                <pb facs="0921" n="755" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg755"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 814.48/8</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Thurston to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-12-27T18:00:00-06:02">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 27, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Shocks continue. Water situation becoming serious, sanitary conditions
                    correspondingly affected. Mr. Clark, President local chapter American Red Cross
                    offers funds collected to date for relief work. Amount five hundred dollars.
                    Shall I accept and place disposition Government? Destruction continues and
                    thousands now shelterless. Weather mild, foreign colonies safe. Request
                    acknowledgment every message.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
